%S A400706 0,1,3,1,2,1,6,1,2,2,3,1,3,1,4,1,2,2,1,11,1,2,2,3,2,3,1,4,1,2,4,1,2,2,
%T A400706 1,10,1,2,2,3,1,3,1,4,1,2,4,1,2,2
%N A400706 A version of the building sequence A399633 for positive- and negative-integer numbered plots: this sequence gives the heights of the buildings at nonnegative-numbered plots, in order.
%C A400706 In A399633 the buildings are erected on a semi-infinite row of plots numbered with the positive integers 1, 2, 3, 4, ... In the present sequence the buildings are erected along an infinite row of plots labeled with the integers, in order, at lots 0, 1, -1, 2, -2, 3, -3, ..., using the same rule as in A399633.
%C A400706 This sequence shows the heights of the buildings at plots 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, ...
%H A400706 Jonas Karlsson, <a href="/A400706/a400706.png">pinplot of two-way sequence</a>
%K A400706 nonn,more,new
%O A400706 0,3
%A A400706 _Jonas Karlsson_ and _N. J. A. Sloane_, Oct 04 2026
